# Probe 302n, item c in the author's refined form (a baseline on the 301 tuple;
# CODEX-OPUS-AUTHOR-DOCUMENT-ASSIGN-MERGE-PARENS-20261107-01): the same structure computed first -- pack:
# merge(tst\args; (a: int: 5)), then tst(pack) for tst (int: c 3; int: a) (the author's test; test is a word of the
# language) -- to tell a general acceptance of a structure as the whole arguments (35) from the parse of an inline
# merge.  Entry 7 for 35; 100 + v for another value v (191..195 a refusal: merge, call, implements, convert,
# interpreter).  Nothing here is a norm.
fn: tst (int: c 3; int: a) int
    return: c * 10 + a
end: tst
fn: held () int
    ---
        pack: merge(tst\args; (a: int: 5))
        int: got tst(pack)
        return: got
        catch: merge ()
            return: 91
        catch: call ()
            return: 92
        catch: implements ()
            return: 93
        catch: convert ()
            return: 94
        catch: interpreter ()
            return: 95
    ---
end: held
fn: run () int
    int: got held()
    if: got = 35
        return: 7
    ---
    return: got + 100
end: run
int: code run()
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: code; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
